ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE FRAMEWORK ACT ON THE DEVELOPMENT OF THE ELECTRICAL INDUSTRY

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Framework Act on the Development of the Electrical Industry and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Scope of the Electrical Industry)
"Industries prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 2, subparagraph 2 of the Framework Act on the Development of the Electrical Industry (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means the following industries:
1. Industries related to the production, supply, sale, brokerage, use, and management of electricity;
2. Industries related to the design, construction, supervision, safety management, and diagnosis of electrical installations;
3. Industries related to the design, manufacture, and sale of electrical power equipment and materials constituting electrical installations;
4. Industries that provide new industries and new services by promoting intelligent transformation and advancement of the industries specified in subparagraphs 1 through 3;
5. Other ancillary industries necessary for the industries specified in subparagraphs 1 through 4.

Article 3 (Events Commemorating Electricity Day)
The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment or the head of a local government may hold the following events to commemorate Electricity Day pursuant to Article 5 (2) of the Act: <Amended 2025.10.1>
1. Awards for persons or organizations that have contributed to the development of the electrical industry;
2. Academic conferences and international exchange events to promote the electrical industry;
3. Other publicity events to support and foster the electrical industry, etc.

Article 4 (Formulation of Master Plans for the Development of the Electrical Industry, etc.)
(1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall formulate a master plan for the development of the electrical industry under Article 7 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "master plan") by December 31 of the year preceding the year in which the master plan begins. <Amended 2025.10.1>
(2) The heads of relevant central administrative agencies shall prepare sectoral plans related to matters under their respective jurisdiction for the formulation of a master plan and submit them to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment by September 30 of the year preceding the year in which the master plan begins. <Amended 2025.10.1>
(3) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may, in consultation with the heads of relevant central administrative agencies, establish guidelines for preparing sectoral plans under paragraph (2) and notify the heads of relevant central administrative agencies thereof. <Amended 2026.7.21>
(4) Where sectoral plans submitted pursuant to paragraph (2) overlap or conflict with one another, the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may request the heads of relevant central administrative agencies to revise, supplement, or adjust their sectoral plans. <Amended 2025.10.1>
(5) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall consolidate the sectoral plans submitted pursuant to paragraph (2) (including those revised, supplemented, or adjusted pursuant to paragraph (4)), prepare a draft master plan, and notify the heads of relevant central administrative agencies thereof to collect their opinions. <Amended 2025.10.1>
(6) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment deems it necessary to reflect the opinions collected pursuant to paragraph (5), the Minister shall revise the draft master plan and finalize the master plan following deliberation by the Electricity Policy Deliberation Council under Article 47-2 of the Electric Utility Act. <Amended 2025.10.1>
(7) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 7 (2) 8 of the Act means the following: <Amended 2025.10.1>
1. Matters concerning promotion of convergence between the electrical industry and other industries;
2. Matters concerning promotion of digital transformation of the electrical industry;
3. Other matters that the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment deems necessary for the sustainable development of the electrical industry.
(8) "Where minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree are amended" in the proviso to Article 7 (3) of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where matters that do not affect the objectives or direction of a master plan and for which the grounds for amendment are clear are amended;
2. Where errors in calculation, typographical errors, omissions, or equivalent obvious errors are corrected.
(9) "Relevant institutions and organizations prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 7 (4) of the Act means the following institutions and organizations: <Amended 2026.7.21>
1. The Federation of the Korean Electrical Industry under Article 17 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Federation");
2. Public institutions under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions;
3. The Korea Electrical Safety Corporation under Article 30 of the Electrical Safety Management Act;
4. An association of electrical contractors under Article 25 of the Electrical Construction Business Act;
5. An association of electric power engineers under Article 18 of the Electric Technology Management Act.

Article 5 (Formulation of Implementation Plans)
(1) Where a master plan has been formulated, the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment and the heads of relevant central administrative agencies shall formulate annual implementation plans for their respective fields of jurisdiction. <Amended 2025.10.1>
(2) The heads of relevant central administrative agencies shall submit the implementation plans for the current year by the end of February each year, and the preceding year's implementation performance under the implementation plans by the end of May each year, to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended 2025.10.1>

Article 6 (Subjects and Methods of Fact-Finding Surveys, etc.)
(1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may conduct an annual fact-finding survey on the electrical industry (hereinafter referred to as a "fact-finding survey") of business operators related to the electrical industry, etc. pursuant to Article 8 (1) of the Act. <Amended 2025.10.1>
(2) A fact-finding survey shall include the following matters: <Amended 2025.10.1>
1. Matters concerning domestic and overseas market trends and prospects for the electrical industry;
2. Sales performance and the status of imports and exports in the electrical industry;
3. The status of employment in the electrical industry and the status of business operators and workers by field and gender;
4. The status of research, development, and technology related to the electrical industry;
5. Other matters that the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment deems necessary to survey for the formulation and implementation of policies for the sustainable development of the electrical industry.
(3) A fact-finding survey shall be conducted through field surveys, written surveys, literature surveys, etc., and may use electronic means such as information and communications networks or electronic mail.
(4) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment intends to conduct a fact-finding survey, the Minister shall prepare a survey plan including the purpose, period, items, and contents of the survey and the scope of publication of the survey results, etc., and notify the persons subject to the survey in advance. <Amended 2025.10.1>
(5) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment has conducted a fact-finding survey, the Minister may post the results on the website of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended 2025.10.1>

Article 7 (Payment, Use, and Management of Contributions or Support Funds, etc.)
(1) Pursuant to Article 9 (2) of the Act, the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may contribute or provide support for all or part of the costs necessary to implement projects for the research, development, demonstration, and dissemination of electrical technology where all of the following requirements are met: <Amended 2025.10.1>
1. The relevant corporation, institution, or organization shall be a public institution, university, corporation, or organization related to the research, development, etc. of electrical technology (including their affiliated research institutes, etc.; hereinafter referred to as "electrical technology research institutions");
2. The project plan and budget execution plan for the relevant project shall be appropriate.
(2) A person who receives contributions or support funds under paragraph (1) shall manage those contributions or support funds in a separate account and use them only for projects for the research, development, demonstration, and dissemination of electrical technology, as determined by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended 2025.10.1>

Article 8 (Institutions for Training a Specialized Workforce for the Electrical Industry)
"Institutions or organizations related to the electrical industry prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10 (2) 3 of the Act means the following institutions or organizations: <Amended 2025.10.1>
1. Government-funded research institutions under the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Research Institutes;
2. Government-funded research institutions in the field of science and technology under the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Science and Technology Research Institutes;
3. Universities with departments, faculties, or equivalent organizational units or majors related to the electrical field among schools under Article 2 of the Higher Education Act;
4. Other institutions or organizations recognized and publicly notified by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment as necessary for training a specialized workforce for the electrical industry.

Article 9 (Procedures for Designation of Specialized Workforce Training Institutions, etc.)
(1) A person who intends to be designated as a specialized workforce training institution under Article 10 (2) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment an application for designation as a specialized workforce training institution, as publicly notified by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment, together with the following documents: <Amended 2025.10.1>
1. Articles of incorporation or equivalent business operating regulations;
2. Performance records and plans for education, professional development, research, training, etc. in the field of the electrical industry (hereinafter referred to as "education, etc.");
3. The current status of facilities, personnel, and equipment secured for education, etc.;
4. A plan for procuring annual operating expenses and a plan for utilizing support funds.
(2) The contents of education, etc. under Article 10 (4) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended 2025.10.1>
1. Matters concerning the structure and current status of the electrical industry;
2. Matters concerning laws and systems related to the electrical industry;
3. Matters concerning safety management in the electrical industry;
4. Matters concerning specialized technologies necessary for the electrical industry;
5. Matters concerning new industries and new services through the digital transformation, intelligent transformation, and advancement of the electrical industry;
6. Other matters necessary for the sustainable development of the electrical industry that are determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment.

Article 10 (Management of Specialized Workforce Training Institutions)
(1) The head of an institution designated as a specialized workforce training institution pursuant to Article 10 (2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "specialized workforce training institution") shall prepare and submit to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment each year a plan for education, etc. of a specialized workforce for the electrical industry for the following year (hereinafter referred to as an "education plan"). <Amended 2025.10.1>
(2) An education plan shall include the following matters:
1. The basic direction of education, etc.;
2. Subjects, duration, and expected number of participants for education, etc.;
3. Criteria and plans for selecting participants in education, etc.;
4. Methods of assessing performance in education, etc.;
5. Measures for procuring financial resources for education, etc. and plans for their utilization;
6. Other matters necessary for education, etc. of a specialized workforce for the electrical industry.
(3) To provide efficient education, etc., the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may conduct inspections or evaluations of the facilities, courses of education, etc., operational conditions, etc. of specialized workforce training institutions. <Amended 2025.10.1>
(4) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment conducts an inspection or evaluation under paragraph (3), the Minister shall notify the head of the specialized workforce training institution of the results. <Amended 2025.10.1>

Article 11 (Support for Specialized Workforce Training Institutions)
(1) Pursuant to Article 10 (3) of the Act, the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may provide specialized workforce training institutions with support for all or part of the following costs within the budget: <Amended 2025.10.1>
1. Costs of developing materials for education, etc. and purchasing equipment and materials for practical training;
2. Instructors' lecture fees and allowances;
3. Costs of installing and operating facilities for education, etc.;
4. Costs of field training;
5. Other costs deemed necessary for training a specialized workforce.
(2) A specialized workforce training institution that receives support under paragraph (1) shall manage the support funds in a separate account and use them only for the costs specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1).

Article 12 (Support for International Cooperation and Entry into Overseas Markets)
(1) Pursuant to Article 11 (2) of the Act, the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may support international exchanges of technology and personnel, international standardization, and international joint research and development projects related to the electrical industry undertaken by the following institutions or organizations: <Amended 2025.10.1, 2026.7.21>
1. The Federation;
2. The association of electrical contractors under Article 25 of the Electrical Construction Business Act;
3. The association of electric power engineers under Article 18 of the Electric Technology Management Act;
4. Corporations established pursuant to the Civil Act or another Act that the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment recognizes as possessing expertise in the field of the electrical industry.
(2) The scope of support under paragraph (1) shall be as follows: <Amended 2025.10.1>
1. International exchanges of information, technology, and personnel related to the electrical industry;
2. Publicity, such as exhibitions related to the electrical industry, and overseas marketing;
3. International joint research and development projects related to the electrical industry;
4. Collection, analysis, and provision of information concerning overseas expansion related to the electrical industry;
5. Other projects deemed necessary by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment for securing the international competitiveness of the electrical industry.

Article 13 (Details of Projects to Promote Digital Transformation of the Electrical Industry)
(1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may have an electrical technology research institution conduct the following projects related to promoting the digital transformation of the electrical industry (hereinafter referred to as "digital transformation promotion projects") pursuant to Article 13 (2) of the Act: <Amended on October 1, 2025>

1. Developing and disseminating digital innovation models utilizing information and data from the electrical industry;

2. Establishing infrastructure for the digital transformation of the electrical industry;

3. Other projects that the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment deems to require support for the digital transformation of the electrical industry.

(2) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment intends to have an electrical technology research institution conduct a digital transformation promotion project pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister shall take the following matters into consideration: <Amended on October 1, 2025>

1. The validity and feasibility of the digital transformation promotion project;

2. The capacity to conduct the digital transformation promotion project, including the level of technology and personnel possessed by the electrical technology research institution;

3. The social and economic ripple effects of the digital transformation promotion project.

Article 14 (Support for Costs Necessary to Conduct Digital Transformation Promotion Projects)
(1) An electrical technology research institution seeking support under Article 13 (3) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment the basis for calculating the costs necessary to implement the digital transformation promotion project. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

(2) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may review the basis for calculation submitted pursuant to paragraph (1) and provide support for all or part of the costs necessary to conduct the digital transformation promotion project. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

(3) An electrical technology research institution that receives support under paragraph (2) shall manage the support funds in a separate account and use them only to cover the costs necessary for the relevant digital transformation promotion project.

Article 15 (Entrustment of Duties concerning Technical Standards for the Electrical Industry)
(1) "An institution or organization meeting the criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 15 (2) of the Act means an institution or organization meeting all of the following criteria:

1. It shall be a corporation, institution, or organization that performs duties related to the electrical industry;

2. The scope of its activities under the articles of association or rules of the relevant corporation, institution, or organization shall include duties related to technical standards for the electrical industry;

3. It shall have a dedicated organizational unit and personnel for establishing, managing, and operating technical standards for the electrical industry.

(2) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment entrusts duties concerning the establishment, management, and operation of technical standards to a corporation, institution, or organization under paragraph (1) pursuant to Article 15 (2) of the Act, the Minister shall publicly notify the person entrusted with the duties and the details of the entrusted duties. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

(3) A person who receives support for the costs necessary to conduct entrusted projects pursuant to Article 15 (2) of the Act shall manage the support funds in a separate account and use them only for purposes relating to the establishment, management, and operation of technical standards.

Article 16 (Composition and Operation of an Inter-Institutional Consultative Body for the Electrical Industry)
(1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may organize and operate a consultative body (hereinafter referred to as the "Electrical Industry Consultative Council") to consult with relevant administrative agencies, local governments, corporations, and organizations on the following matters pursuant to Article 16 (1) of the Act: <Amended on October 1, 2025>

1. Matters concerning policies and projects related to the electrical industry;

2. Matters concerning the development of electrical technology, the training of specialized workforce, and job creation related to the electrical industry;

3. Matters concerning public-private cooperation related to subparagraphs 1 and 2;

4. Other matters deemed necessary for formulating policies, etc. for the sustainable development of the electrical industry.

(2) The Electrical Industry Consultative Council shall consist of not more than 30 members, including one chairperson.

(3) The chairperson of the Electrical Industry Consultative Council shall be a person designated by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment from among public officials in the Senior Civil Service who perform duties related to the electrical industry at the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment, and its members shall be the following persons: <Amended on October 1, 2025; December 30, 2025; July 21, 2026>

1. Persons designated by the heads of the relevant central administrative agencies from among public officials of Grade IV or higher responsible for duties related to the electrical industry at the Ministry of Finance and Economy, the Ministry of Science and ICT, the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, the Ministry of Planning and Budget, and the National Fire Agency;

2. Persons designated by the relevant Special City Mayor, Integrated Special City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayor, Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governor, or Special Self-Governing Province Governor from among public officials of Grade V or higher performing duties related to the electrical industry at a Special City, Integrated Special City, Metropolitan City, Special Self-Governing City, Do, or Special Self-Governing Province;

3. Persons commissioned by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment from among persons with extensive knowledge and experience in the electrical industry who belong to any of the following institutions or organizations:

(a) An association of electrical contractors under Article 25 of the Electrical Construction Business Act;

(b) An association of electric power engineers under Article 18 of the Electric Technology Management Act;

(c) A government-funded research institute under the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Research Institutes;

(d) A government-funded science and technology research institute under the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Science and Technology Research Institutes;

(e) A corporation established pursuant to the Civil Act or another Act that the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment recognizes as having expertise in the electrical industry.

(4) The term of office of a member under paragraph (3) 3 shall be two years, and the member may be recommissioned only once.

(5) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may provide support for the expenses necessary to operate the Electrical Industry Consultative Council within budgetary limits. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

Article 17 (Matters to Be Included in the Articles of Association of the Federation)
(1) The articles of association of the Federation shall include the following matters: <Amended on July 21, 2026>

1. Purpose;

2. Name;

3. Location of the principal office;

4. Details of activities;

5. Qualifications for membership;

6. The prescribed number, terms of office, and methods of election of executive officers;

7. Composition of the general meeting and matters subject to its resolutions;

8. Composition of the board of directors and matters subject to its resolutions;

9. Matters concerning assets and accounting;

10. Procedures for amending the articles of association.

(2) The Federation shall perform the following duties: <Amended on July 21, 2026>

1. Survey and research concerning the development of the electrical industry and the efficient performance of duties;

2. Duties to improve the competitiveness of the electrical industry;

3. Preparation of measures to develop policies and systems related to the electrical industry;

4. Duties entrusted pursuant to statutes and regulations;

5. Other duties prescribed by the articles of association for the development of the electrical industry and the efficient performance of duties.

Article 18 (Procedures for Authorization of Establishment of the Federation)
(1) To establish the Federation pursuant to Article 17 (1) of the Act, at least 50 business operators related to the electrical industry or heads of relevant institutions or organizations shall act as promoters, prepare the articles of association, and apply to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment for authorization following a resolution of the inaugural general meeting. <Amended on October 1, 2025; July 21, 2026>

(2) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment grants authorization of establishment under paragraph (1), the Minister shall post that fact on the website of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

(3) Where the Federation intends to amend any of the matters specified in the subparagraphs of Article 17 (1), it shall apply to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment for authorization of the amendment within 10 days from the date on which the general meeting that adopted the resolution on the amendment concluded. <Amended on October 1, 2025; July 21, 2026>

(4) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment authorizes an amendment to the name of the Federation or the location of its principal office among the matters subject to authorization of amendments under paragraph (3), the Minister shall post that fact on the website of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on October 1, 2025; July 21, 2026>

Article 19 (Supervision of the Federation)
(1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall supervise the affairs of the Federation. <Amended on October 1, 2025; July 21, 2026>

(2) Where necessary to supervise the Federation, the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may require the Federation to report on matters concerning its affairs or submit materials, and may issue other necessary orders. <Amended on October 1, 2025; July 21, 2026>

(3) The Federation shall submit its business plan and revenue and expenditure budget to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment before the beginning of each fiscal year. <Amended on October 1, 2025; July 21, 2026>

Article 20 (Entrustment of Duties)
(1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may entrust all or part of the following duties to the Federation or to a public institution or organization related to the electrical industry that the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment designates and publicly notifies pursuant to Article 18 (2) of the Act: <Amended on October 1, 2025; July 21, 2026>

1. Survey and research for the formulation of master plans and implementation plans under Article 7 of the Act;

2. Fact-finding surveys under Article 8 (1) of the Act;

3. Duties concerning the payment of contributions and support funds for projects for research, development, demonstration, and dissemination of electrical technology under Article 9 (2) of the Act;

4. Receipt of applications for designation as specialized workforce training institutions and review and confirmation of the details of the applications under Article 10 (2) of the Act;

5. Duties concerning the payment of support funds to specialized workforce training institutions under Article 10 (3) of the Act;

6. Duties concerning support for projects such as international exchanges of technology and personnel related to the electrical industry, international standardization, and international joint research and development under Article 11 (2) of the Act;

7. Duties concerning the payment of support funds for digital transformation promotion projects under Article 13 (3) of the Act.

(2) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment entrusts duties pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister shall publicly notify the person entrusted with the duties and the details of the entrusted duties. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 35154, December 31, 2024>

